[
  {
    "id": "PRRT_kwDOQ6DXvM5ye8vs",
    "isResolved": false,
    "comments": {
      "nodes": [
        {
          "databaseId": 2893429251,
          "author": {
            "login": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"
          },
          "body": "This environment-variable list doesn’t match the actual `.env.example` / ConfigService keys used by the API. For example, the code uses `DB_HOST`/`DB_PORT` (not `DATABASE_URL`), `REDIS_HOST`/`REDIS_PORT` (not `REDIS_URL`), `IPFS_LOCAL_API_URL` (not `KUBO_API_URL`), and `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (not `CORS_ORIGINS`). Please align these names with `apps/api/.env.example` and the corresponding config lookups so developers don’t misconfigure local/staging environments.",
          "path": ".planning/codebase/INTEGRATIONS.md",
          "line": 151
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "PRRT_kwDOQ6DXvM5ye8v2",
    "isResolved": false,
    "comments": {
      "nodes": [
        {
          "databaseId": 2893429262,
          "author": {
            "login": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"
          },
          "body": "The “Unit tests” command is misleading: `pnpm test` runs `pnpm --parallel -r run test`, which includes the Playwright E2E workspace (`tests/e2e`), and will attempt to start servers / require infra. Consider changing this section to run only unit-test workspaces (e.g., `pnpm --filter @cipherbox/api test`, `pnpm --filter @cipherbox/web test`, `pnpm --filter @cipherbox/crypto test`) and keep `pnpm test:e2e` for Playwright.\n```suggestion\npnpm --filter @cipherbox/api test\npnpm --filter @cipherbox/web test\npnpm --filter @cipherbox/crypto test\n```",
          "path": "docs/DEVELOPMENT.md",
          "line": 109
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "PRRT_kwDOQ6DXvM5ye8v9",
    "isResolved": false,
    "comments": {
      "nodes": [
        {
          "databaseId": 2893429274,
          "author": {
            "login": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"
          },
          "body": "The key hierarchy claims per-file IPNS keypairs are HKDF-derived from the user private key. However, the implementation supports random per-file IPNS keys for new files (with the ECIES-wrapped private key stored in the FilePointer) alongside legacy HKDF-derived keys. Adjust this block to avoid implying HKDF-derivation is universal for per-file IPNS.",
          "path": ".github/copilot-instructions.md",
          "line": 55
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "PRRT_kwDOQ6DXvM5ye8wF",
    "isResolved": false,
    "comments": {
      "nodes": [
        {
          "databaseId": 2893429284,
          "author": {
            "login": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"
          },
          "body": "The “Planned (v1.1+)” list appears to include features that are already implemented in the repo (e.g., Sharing is implemented via the shares API/controllers and the web ShareDialog/Shared page; Recycle Bin is implemented via BinBrowser/bin services). Either move these into the current Features list or clarify that they’re “planned to productize” rather than “not yet built.”",
          "path": "README.md",
          "line": 33
        }
      ]
    }
  }
]

